      "content": "Take 81mg of aspirin, twice a day, to help thin out the mucus and reduce inflammation. Don't worry about the full adult dose, you're not taking it for pain relief, just to help with congestion. As for the multivitamin and ibuprofen, go for it! Just be sure to take the aspirin at least 30 minutes before the ibuprofen, so you don't interfere with its absorption. And if the heaviness gets worse, you can always take an extra dose of aspirin.",
